{number: 127}
{title: I Am Coming, Lord}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I hear Thy welcome voice,
That calls me, [G7] Lord, to [C] Thee
For cleansing in Thy [F] precious blood
That [C] flowed on [G7] Calva-[C] ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] I am coming, Lord!
[G7] Coming now to [C] Thee!
Wash me, cleanse me in the [F] blood
That [C] flowed on [G7] Calva-[C] ry!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Tho' [C] coming weak and vile,
Thou dost my [G7] strength as-[C] sure;
Thou dost my vileness [F] fully cleanse,
Till [C] spotless [G7] all and [C] pure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
'Tis [C] Jesus calls me on
To perfect [G7] faith and [C] love,
To perfect hope, and [F] peace, and trust,
For [C] earth and [G7] heav'n a-[C] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
'Tis [C] Jesus who confirms
The blessed [G7] work with-[C] in,
By adding grace to [F] welcomed grace,
Where [C] reigned the [G7] pow'r of [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}
